# Public site chrome (raynuv.com)

The look and feel of `https://raynuv.com` is the **site-updater** design merged in PRs **#218–#226** (Syne + Source Serif, CIO View, Stories mast, COM2, HDA tracker). That chrome lives on **`main`**.

## Do

- Put **stories / CIO copy / HDA notes** on a **site PR against `main`** (not on ISO/E5/SPA feature branches).
- Keep `site/hda.json` generated only by `./tools/sync-hda-site.sh` from `docs/hda.md` frontmatter.
- On Everest-path feature branches, merge `origin/main -- site/` if Cloudflare might build that branch — never ship a truncated `site/` tree.
- Production Worker deploys from **`main` only** (`.github/workflows/worker.yml` + `./tools/lock-cloudflare-production-branch.sh`).

## Do not

- Restyle `site/index.html`, `site/styles.css`, `site/stories.html`, `site/ciospeak.html`, or `site/com2.html` while working on hypervisor/ISO/SPA code.
- Delete `ciospeak.html`, `com2.html`, responsive `site/assets/*.webp`, or the CIO/Stories nav.
- Point Cloudflare Git production at a feature branch. Non-production builds must not `wrangler deploy` over the live Worker.
- Claim `RAYNU-V-M7-ISO-INSTALL-OK` from nested QEMU, host tests, or CI. Nested RayNu-F reboot-to-disk is not iron E5.

## Check

```bash
./tools/check-site-chrome.sh
./tools/sync-hda-site.sh --check
```
